       fhir:PlanDefinition.action.textEquivalent [ fhir:value "Possible methods include: Levonorgestrel IUD, copper IUD, implants, LAM, oral contraceptive pills, sterilization, tubal ligation	\n\nNote: LAM is an effective method for breastfeeding women who are amenorrhoeic and their infant < 6 months of age; \n\nBreastfeeding women < 6 weeks postpartum are generally advised not to use injectables and should not use combined hormonal contraceptive (CHC); \n\nBreastfeeding women ≥ 6 weeks can use injectables without restriction; Breastfeeding women ≥ 6 weeks to < 6 months postpartum (primarily breastfeeding) generally should not use CHCs unless other more appropriate methods are not available or acceptable (16)." ] ;
